// Type checking for JavaScript, from the JSDoc that is already here.
//
// Nothing is compiled and nothing is emitted: this reads main.js, preload.js and src/ with the
// annotations they already carry (293 of them across 41 files when this was added) and says where
// the code and its own documentation disagree. The first run found a require that had never
// resolved, two handlers that answered every call with "Cannot find module", and three pieces of
// JSDoc that described a different function than the one below them.
//
// Why these settings:
//   checkJs with strict off - the point is to catch what is wrong today, not to fail on every
//     value that could be null. A strict pass over thirty thousand lines written without types
//     reports hundreds of theoretical nulls and teaches everyone to ignore the tool. Tighten it
//     when the easy errors are gone, one flag at a time.
//   module preserve - the app is both now: main.js and the JS modules require, the modules moved
//     to TypeScript import, and some of those use import.meta. CommonJS rejected the last, and
//     preserve reads each file the way it is written. Resolution is bundler's, which finds a
//     require('./x') the way Node does.
//   allowImportingTsExtensions - the modules already moved to TypeScript are required by their
//     .ts name, which is how Node finds them. Their own checking is src/tsconfig.json, strict.
//   esModuleInterop - those modules import Node's own the ES way (import fs from 'node:fs'), and
//     this project reads them too, through the requires that reach them.
//   skipLibCheck - Electron's own .d.ts is not this project's to fix.
//
// Not covered: renderer/ and tools/. The renderer is ES modules against the DOM, the tools are a
// mix of both, and each needs its own settings. Worth doing, one at a time, rather than one
// configuration that fits none of them.
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "allowJs": true,
    "checkJs": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "target": "ES2022",
    "module": "preserve",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "strict": false,
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  "include": ["main.js", "preload.js", "preload-uninstall.js", "src/**/*.js"]
}
